children.desc:
The **League of Nations** was set up after the First World War to **keep peace**. It failed because:

- it had **no army** of its own to enforce decisions;
- the **USA** never joined;
- aggressors simply **walked out**: Japan and Germany left in 1933, Italy later;
- it could not stop **Japan** (Manchuria), **Italy** (Abyssinia) or **Germany**.
